@startuml mailbox-delivery
!theme plain
title Mailbox delivery (v1.3): the agent never reads the carrier; the broker verifies, the decision guard checks against grants, the doorbell rings, the agent fetches body + verification record; outbound is signed by the keeper

database "Carrier\n(Matrix / XMPP)" as MX
participant "Carrier provider\n(child process)" as MP
participant "Bridge core\n(trust gate)" as BR
participant "Trust\n(keys, grants, revocation)" as T
participant "Decision guard\n(small local model)" as DG
database "Mailbox\n(bodies + verification records)" as MB
participant "Session host\n(admission, dispatcher)" as SH
participant "Agent\n(OS user a_7)" as A
participant "Key keeper" as KK

== inbound ==
MX -> MP: event addressed to agent a_7
MP -> MP: persist (fsync); advance cursor
MP -> BR: envelope bytes
BR -> T: signature over exact bytes? key pinned? grant "write to a_7"?\nfresh, no replay, binding current?
alt unsigned or unknown key
  BR -> MB: quarantine body (no verification record)
  BR -> SH: enqueue(doorbell: channel, claimed sender, id)
else signed by a pinned key with the grant
  BR -> DG: {body, sender grants, addressee grant spec}
  DG -> DG: does the request fit the sender's grants towards a_7?\ninjection patterns? → verdict go | no-go, reasons
  DG -> MB: record {body_sha256, sender, grants used, model version, verdict, fingerprint}
  alt no-go
    BR -> SH: enqueue(notice: refused by guard, fingerprint) (host_authored)
  else go
    BR -> SH: enqueue(doorbell + verification record ref, authoritative if the grant allows user_turn)
  end
end
SH -> SH: admit() again; durable inbox; dispatch at a turn boundary
SH -> A: stdin: "validated message <id> from <sender>: fetch from mailbox"\n(or the user turn itself when the grant allows it)

== fetch and re-verify ==
A -> MB: inbox read <id> (tool; binding grant; session token)
MB --> A: body + verification record (who, which grant, what was checked, fingerprint)
A -> A: optional second verification with the same library\n("security is never too much")

== outbound ==
A -> BR: post <binding> <text> (tool; rate-limited; audited)
BR -> BR: audience projection for the room
BR -> KK: sign(bytes) on behalf of a_7 (peer UID = bridge; identity a_7 bound)
KK --> BR: signature
BR -> MP: output{signed metadata, text}
MP -> MX: post; people see ordinary text, the signature rides in metadata
@enduml
